----------------------------- Recursion -----------------------------------
Recursion:- Recursion is the process where a function calls itself directly or indirectly.

💡 Core Components of a Recursive Function:
To prevent the function from calling itself infinitely and crashing the program (causing a Stack Overflow error), every recursive function must have two main parts:
• Base Case: The condition under which the function stops calling itself and returns a definitive value.
• Recursive Case: The part of the function where it modifies its parameters and calls itself to solve a smaller sub-problem.

🧩 Classic Example: Factorial of a Number (n!)

int factorial(int n) {
    // 1. Base Case
    if (n == 1 || n == 0) {
        return 1;
    }

    // 2. Recursive Case
    return n * factorial(n - 1);
}

Note: Base Case/Stopping Condition / Termination Condition/Exit Condition/Anchor Case/Ground Case / Bottom-up Limit/Trivial Case
----------------------------- Global Variables ----------------------------
Preference:
Local variable > static/class variable when both have the same name.

Aur static x ko specifically access karna ho to:
ClassName.x
Eg: System.out.println(Test.x); where Test is a className


static = class ke saath associated, but value change ho sakti hai.      //Class ke saath associated means: static variable object ke saath nahi, balki class ke saath belong karta hai.
final = value change nahi ho sakti.


Normal variable → Object ka hai
static variable → Class ka hai
Eg: static int x = 10;        // ✅ change allowed
    static final int x = 10;  // ❌ change not allowed


------------------ Find Power --------------------
1st: Linear Recursion (Naive Recursive Exponentiation):     [TC: O(b), AS: O(b)]
pow(a,b) = a*pow(a, b-1)

2nd: Optimized Recursion [Exponentiation by Squaring (Fast Exponentiation / Binary Exponentiation)]:        [TC: O(log b), AS: O(log b)]        =>Recommended
pow(a,b) = call*call        =>when b is even        Where, call = pow(a, b/2)
         = a*call*call      =>when b is odd


Que: Why is called Linear Recursion?
Ans: Because in every recursive call, the exponent decreases by 1:

----------------------------- Formula ----------------------
Sum of natural numbers(1+2+3+...+ n-2 + n-1 +n): n*(n+1)/2
Sum of cubes of natural numbers(1^3 +2^3 +3^3 +...+ (n-2)^3 + (n-1)^3 +n^3) : [n(n+1)/2]^2
                                                                            : [n^2*(n+1)^2]4

